L33|Even so, the company was still growing everywhere else. In twenty twelve it had eighty million users worldwide.
L34|Its own chief executive said it out loud. We have roughly eighty million users today. Nokia doesn't have that.
L35|But being big is not the same as being wanted. The market was leaving while the number of users was still rising.
L36|In October twenty eleven the network failed. For days, email and messages were down across five continents.
L37|It happened exactly as Apple was launching the iPhone 4S. The failure could not have been timed worse.
L38|In early twenty twelve, the two men who had run the company for two decades stepped down. Thorsten Heins took over.
